From: Stoicoci Mihaita <stoicocimihaita@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] q706f: dts: disable the unused PCIe2 (modem) root port

lspci shows only the root bridge on domain 0002; the controller is
runtime-active with gcc_pcie_2_* clocks, the QMP PHY and pcie_2_gdsc on.
qcom-pcie powers a link-less controller down in suspend_noirq, so this is
an awake/idle saving, not an s2idle one.

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8250-lenovo-q706f.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8250-lenovo-q706f.dts
index 4855787d0a102922be7f3bc41e8fc5e7623a8247..8417eaa60c3d82785f5083ae79c3654da1ae078b 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8250-lenovo-q706f.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8250-lenovo-q706f.dts
@@ -1194,14 +1194,20 @@ wifi@0 {
 	};
 };
 
+/*
+ * PCIe2 is the SDX55 modem link of the 5G variant (TB-Q706Z). Nothing is
+ * attached on the Wi-Fi-only TB-Q706F: the root port has no device behind it,
+ * yet the controller, its PHY, eight GCC clocks and pcie_2_gdsc stay active
+ * for as long as the tablet is awake. Re-enable for TB-Q706Z modem work.
+ */
 &pcie2 {
-	status = "okay";
+	status = "disabled";
 };
 
 &pcie2_phy {
 	vdda-phy-supply = <&vreg_l5a_0p88>;
 	vdda-pll-supply = <&vreg_l9a_1p2>;
-	status = "okay";
+	status = "disabled";
 };
 
 &pm8150b_adc {
